      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search copies the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Any quote in the name ends the string literal and lets the caller add SQL. Any caller of GET /users can read or change any data the database user can reach. Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search copies the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Any quote in the name ends the string literal and lets the caller add SQL.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can read or change any data the database user can reach.",
      "fix": "Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex stays locked when key is missing",
      "description": "Count takes h.mu and then returns early when key is empty. That path never releases h.mu. A single request to GET /count with no key blocks every later Count request forever. Those requests pile up as stuck goroutines. Check key before taking the lock, or release the lock with defer right after Lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count takes h.mu and then returns early when key is empty. That path never releases h.mu.",
      "consequence": "A single request to GET /count with no key blocks every later Count request forever. Those requests pile up as stuck goroutines.",
      "fix": "Check key before taking the lock, or release the lock with defer right after Lock."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Response body closed before the error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil. Every request to GET /upstream panics while the upstream is unreachable, so the caller never gets the 502 response. Move the deferred Close below the error check.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil.",
      "consequence": "Every request to GET /upstream panics while the upstream is unreachable, so the caller never gets the 502 response.",
      "fix": "Move the deferred Close below the error check."
    },
